# Project Constraints

- Do not change application functionality unless the user explicitly asks for a behavior change.
- Treat existing rendering, file parsing, frame processing, math, output generation, and keyboard workflows as behavior to preserve during migration.
- LaserBoy is being transformed into a GUI-first editor, not kept as a permanently optional GUI layer over the old app.
- Keep the TUI/keyboard system for now as command compatibility and shortcuts; later it should be pared down to interaction commands while file operations, options, settings, stats, and status move into GUI regions.
- New GUI regions should call into existing app/core logic instead of replacing or duplicating it.
- Prefer routing new GUI buttons and menu items through existing keyboard command paths when those commands already exist.
- Keep changes tightly scoped. Avoid broad refactors unless they directly support the GUI-first architecture.
- Refactor core code when needed to expose clean model, command, or rendering interfaces, and keep those refactors behavior-preserving.
- When building or validating changes, default to building the GUI version unless a non-GUI build is needed for targeted troubleshooting; after that troubleshooting, finish with a GUI build.
